    "diagnosis": "The bit-counting loop iterates one index beyond the legal mask range and uses a right-shift width that collapses to zero on the first iteration, so every non-zero tkeep is misclassified as the minimum frame length. Consequently the frame length register accumulates three bytes over cycles 2\u20134 instead of resetting at the frame boundary, producing a value of 3 when the oracle expects the new frame\u2019s first-byte count of 1 at cycle 5.",
